1	/**
2	 * The eight things that travel down a generation, as the browser types them.
3	 *
4	 * Written by hand, exactly as `WorldView` was, because the server's description
5	 * of itself and this canvas are built at the same time. The server's own copy is
6	 * `backend/src/katalyst/engine/events.py`; a later pull request pins the two
7	 * against each other with a type-level test, so that neither can drift.
8	 *
9	 * **Field names are the wire's, in full.** `input_tokens`, not `inputTokens`. A
10	 * second spelling of a field is a second thing that can drift, and these come
11	 * straight off the stream and are printed straight onto the screen. The browser's
12	 * own view model, `WorldView`, keeps its own spellings because it is a different
13	 * thing with a different life.
14	 *
15	 * **Two facts the eight deliberately do not carry twice.** Whether a destination
16	 * was reached is on the verdict and nowhere else — the reason a *generation*
17	 * stopped is a different question with a different answer. And whether the run
18	 * was live or played back, the day a recording was made and the fingerprint of
19	 * the prompt are on the receipt and nowhere else. Two places to read one fact
20	 * eventually disagree.
21	 *
22	 * **One fact they do carry twice, and it is not the same mistake.** The set of
23	 * claims still open rides on both growth events. It is not one fact worked out
24	 * two ways; it is one fact restated after every change to it, so that whichever
25	 * event arrives is enough on its own to redraw the reserved rectangles.
26	 */
